From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:47:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] damageext: set the drawable of a new Damage object

ProcDamageCreate never stored the request's drawable in the DamageExtRec,
and DamageExtNotify copies that field into every DamageNotify event, so
the events carried whatever malloc left there (0 here).  A compositing
manager could not tell which window was damaged: xcompmgr looked the
events up by drawable, found nothing, and never repainted.
---
 damageext/damageext.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/damageext/damageext.c b/damageext/damageext.c
index 3c34ebc..a1bda14 100644
--- a/damageext/damageext.c
+++ b/damageext/damageext.c
@@ -210,6 +210,7 @@ ProcDamageCreate(ClientPtr client)
     if (!pDamageExt)
         return BadAlloc;
     pDamageExt->id = stuff->damage;
+    pDamageExt->drawable = stuff->drawable;
     pDamageExt->pDrawable = pDrawable;
     pDamageExt->level = level;
     pDamageExt->pClient = client;
